From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: a duplicated frame says it has a dirty rectangle (TotalMetadataBufferSize)

0012's AcquireNextFrame left DXGI_OUTDUPL_FRAME_INFO's TotalMetadataBufferSize
at 0 although GetFrameDirtyRects then gives the whole output. On Windows it
is the size of the frame's move and dirty rectangles, and programs read the
rectangles -- and copy the picture -- only when it is not 0: TightVNC's
Desktop Duplication capture (UseD3D, its default) copied nothing, and its
viewers saw a black screen (i0633; its GDI capture was fine). It is now one
RECT: no move rectangle, the output as the dirty one.
---
diff --git a/src/dxgi/dxgi_output_dup.cpp b/src/dxgi/dxgi_output_dup.cpp
index 50cf379..ffc38ca 100644
--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_output_dup.cpp
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_output_dup.cpp
@@ -177,6 +177,14 @@ namespace dxvk {
         QueryPerformanceCounter(&now);
         pFrameInfo->LastPresentTime   = now;
         pFrameInfo->AccumulatedFrames = 1;
+        /* the bytes of this frame's move and dirty rectangles: no move
+         * rectangle, the whole output as the one dirty rectangle. A
+         * program reads the rectangles only when this says there are
+         * some -- TightVNC's duplication copied nothing, and its viewer
+         * stayed black, while it was 0 */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DXVKDUP_NO_METADATA
+        pFrameInfo->TotalMetadataBufferSize = sizeof(RECT);
+#endif
 
         HRESULT hr = m_texture->QueryInterface(__uuidof(IDXGIResource),
           reinterpret_cast<void**>(ppDesktopResource));
